  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/199) by Michael Ezra (Bitbucket: [Michael Ezra](https://bitbucket.org/Michael Ezra), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nWhen zoomed in, the moment user clicks the preview with the Hand tool or zoomes in, the preview first becomes pixelated, and only after that gets rendered into its final high quality state.\n\nThis is I think a result of the technical debt and is not the feature that is user-friendly.\n\n1. In the short term, would it be possible, to avoid such pixelisation while dragging and zooming? \n2. Ultimately, if this can become fluid this would significantly improve the feel of the software.\n\n‌\n",
